Glow Up & Co. – Changelog

This file records the changes and improvements made to the Glow Up & Co. website during development.

Part 3 – Enhancing Functionality and SEO

Changes made

* Reviewed and improved the HTML structure of the website pages.
* Added SEO page titles and meta descriptions.
* Checked that each page has a suitable main heading.
* Added descriptive alt text to website images to improve accessibility and image understanding.
* Created a JavaScript booking form.
* Added JavaScript functionality to display a confirmation message after a valid booking request.
* Added date validation to prevent customers from selecting past booking dates.
* Created and updated the README.md file to document the project.
* Added an interactive Google Maps embed to the Contact Us & Bookings page.
* Implemented a gallery lightbox allowing visitors to enlarge images and close the overlay.
* Updated the JavaScript file to support both the booking form and gallery lightbox without interfering with each other.
* Tested the booking form, gallery lightbox, interactive map and mobile responsiveness.
* Created a separate enquiry page (enquiry.html).
* Added customer details, service selection, preferred appointment date and enquiry message fields.
* Implemented JavaScript validation and personalised confirmation messages.
* Created a separate enquiry page (enquiry.html).
* Added customer details, service selection, preferred appointment date and enquiry message fields.
* Implemented JavaScript validation and personalised confirmation messages.
* Added a general contact form to contact.html.
* Implemented HTML5 and JavaScript form validation.
* Added personalised confirmation messages after successful submissions.
* Styled the general contact form to match the website branding.
* Integrated Formspree for enquiry form email submissions.
* Integrated Formspree for general contact form email submissions.
* Implemented asynchronous form submission using JavaScript Fetch API.
* Added error handling for unsuccessful submissions and connection problems.
* Added robots.txt to the project root.
* Created sitemap.xml containing all six website pages.
* Added lazy loading and asynchronous decoding to website images.
* Compressed selected website images.
* Confirmed that form submissions use HTTPS through Formspree.
* Tested booking, enquiry and contact form functionality.
* Added honeypot spam-protection fields to both Formspree forms.
* Tested enquiry and contact form submissions after the update.
* Documented off-page SEO strategies, including backlinks and social media promotion.
* Added a local SEO strategy suitable for the fictional beauty parlour.
* Included recommendations for future online business listings.
* Reviewed SEO titles and meta descriptions across all six pages.
* Checked heading structure and image alternative text.
* Completed basic SEO and accessibility checks.

